  "snippet": "#​649 — November 26, 2026 Read on the Web Your Tools Are Hiding npm Audits From You — Running npm audit over a fresh Next.js app can show zero vulnerabilities, but a separate audit of its bundled dependencies tells a dif...",
  "coverImage": "https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/v1653576619/lgfqinzbdqttwmhvljxb.png",
  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​649 — November 26, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193470/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; margin: 0; padding: 0;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/v1653576619/lgfqinzbdqttwmhvljxb.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"100%\"/></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193429/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/lk2z5ellvjvtf3fupgrk.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193429/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.zachleat.com\">Your Tools Are Hiding npm Audits From You</a></span> — Running <code>npm audit</code> over a fresh Next.js app can show zero vulnerabilities, but a separate audit of its bundled dependencies tells a different story. Zach shows how Next.js can <em>'sweep audits under the rug'</em> by vendoring dependencies, and has built <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193430/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">📊 Prototype Pollution Report</a> to rank popular frameworks' packages based on their audit results.</p>\n<p>Zach Leatherman </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193428/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"110\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/38679442.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"110\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193428/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"clickhouse.com\">Instant Postgres Branches for Every Agent Run</a></span> — ClickHouse acquired Xata to bring instant branching, cloning, and scale-to-zero to ClickHouse Managed Postgres, now GA on local NVMe and up to 10x faster. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193428/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">Start with $300 in free credits</a>.</p>\n<p>ClickHouse Managed Postgres <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193431/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\"><code>node:sqlite</code> is Now Marked Stable</a></span> — More than two years after its experimental debut, Node's <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193432/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">built-in SQLite module</a> is now marked stable as of <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193433/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">today's latest Node 27 alpha (0.2.0)</a>. No native addon is required.</p>\n<p>Node.js </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>IN BRIEF:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193434/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">AWS Lambda now supports Node.js 26</a> as a managed runtime (for both Web and Event functions) and container base image (for Event Functions only).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>⚠️ Several Fastify plugins have had <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193435/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">a flurry of security fixes</a>, including critical middleware bypasses in <code>@fastify/express</code> and <code>@fastify/middie</code>, and request smuggling in <code>@fastify/reply-from</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>💡 An <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193436/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">open PR proposes adding a built-in pprof CPU profiler</a> to Node, ported from <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193437/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Datadog's work</a>, with reviewers debating the approach.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Node's main branch <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193438/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">now uses Ada 4.1</a>, a <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193439/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">notably faster release</a> of the URL parser behind <code>URL</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🤖 Vercel's <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193440/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">eve</a>, a Next.js-style agent framework we featured in June, <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193441/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">has reached 1.0</a>. The idea is for you to 'own the harness' you build agents on.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🇺🇸 <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193442/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">CascadiaJS 2027</a> is taking place in Seattle next June and <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193443/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">its CFP</a> is open till January 10 (curiously you can even submit your talk via an MCP server!).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193444/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.devas.life\">How I Fixed 55 Bugs in a Week by Making My Monorepo More Agent-Friendly</a></span> — <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193445/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">Inkdrop</a> is a fantastic Electron-based note taking app I've been using for years, so it's cool to see how its creator has reshaped it for his agents to work on. Feature folders, strict lint rules, and new tests added extra discipline, surfacing a variety of long-standing bugs.</p>\n<p>Takuya Matsuyama </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193446/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"evilmartians.com\">Do Agents Really Do Better With TypeScript?</a></span> — It's often claimed types can make coding agents produce better code, but Evil Martians found across three public benchmarks that agents solved comparable JavaScript issues at least as often as TypeScript issues.</p>\n<p>Irina Nazarova (Evil Martians) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193447/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Ranking Languages and Runtimes by MIME Base64 Decoding Speed</a> – Node, Bun and Deno all sit near the top, largely thanks to Daniel's <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193448/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">simdutf</a>. <cite>Daniel Lemire</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193449/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Finding a Memory Leak in a Production NestJS App</a> <cite>Kamil Mysliwiec</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193450/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">5 Steps to Refactor a Fastify App for Testing and Growth</a> <cite>Liran Tal</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>🛠 Code &amp; Tools</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193451/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/pxlcgjtcgl6slnwyvqae.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193451/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"jimp-dev.github.io\">Jimp 2: Image Processing in Plain JavaScript</a></span> — One of the more delightful homepages we've seen! Jimp is a library for working with images in Node or the browser with no native dependencies. After a quiet couple of years, <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193452/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">2.0</a>, <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193453/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">2.1</a> and <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193454/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">2.2</a> landed this week, fixing long-standing quirks and adding <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193455/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">a drawing API</a>. There's a <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193456/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">playground</a> if you want to kick the tires.</p>\n<p>Jimp </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 If you want a smaller option, <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193457/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">ImageScript 4.0</a> can, unlike Jimp, read/write WebP, AVIF and JPEG XL in pure TypeScript, no WASM needed.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193458/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"fingerprint.com\">Anyone Can Claim to Be Claude Duet. Here's How to Spot the Real One</a></span> — A User-Agent header is just text. Fingerprint identifies Claude Duet so you can set rules for login and checkout. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193458/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">Learn how</a>.</p>\n<p>Fingerprint <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193459/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"bloomberg.github.io\">Reintroducing Stricli: Bloomberg's Framework for Type-Safe CLIs</a></span> — Bloomberg builds its internal command line tools with <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193460/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">Stricli</a>. As well as first-class type support (which feeds into auto-generated help and error messages), your commands' code can also be lazy-loaded for added efficiency.</p>\n<p>Michael Molisani and Jeff Posnick (Bloomberg) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193461/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">binary-parser 3.0: Declaratively Build Parsers for Binary Data</a></span> — Chain methods like <code>.uint16be()</code> and <code>.bit4()</code> to describe a binary format, and you end up with a parser as fast as a bespoke one. There are <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193462/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">some examples</a> for parsing ELF, TCP, tar, and similar formats.</p>\n<p>Keichi Takahashi </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193463/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Flatbush 4.9</a> – A fast static spatial index approach for 2D points and rectangles. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193464/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Indexing is now up to 2.7x faster</a> on large inputs.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193465/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">memoize-one 7.0</a> – A memoization library that only caches the result of the most recent arguments.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193466/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">DOMPurify 3.5</a> – Fast XSS sanitizer for HTML, MathML and SVG, usable server-side with <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193467/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">jsdom</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193468/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">ioredis 6.1</a> – Popular performance-focused Redis client.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/193469/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Awilix 14.0</a> – Dependency injection container for Node.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
  "attachments": []
}